{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540500-w20-garou-building-ties-with-the-other-fera","id":1540500,"title":"[W20] Garou building ties with the Other Fera","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-16T00:14:18-07:00","id":1540500,"title":"[W20] Garou building ties with the Other Fera","content":"Maybe it's too hopeful a thing for a WOD game; but I'm.gonna ask it anyway <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> do you think it's possible for Garou Society at large try to build tied with Other Fera?<br /> the gane focus s\u00f3 much on how much the modern Fera hate the Garou Natiom because of the War of Rage.<br /> but hey... wounds cam be headed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T12:40:06-07:00","id":1540523,"title":"","content":"This is metagame issue and not a setting issue for me. The functional purpose of the Fera (besides acknowledging there is other folklore about different animal changers) is to give the Garou other factions that could be either allies or enemies (or even both at the same time). Usually they are intended to be a potential ally that could be won over by the PCs. And because of the divisions between all the Fera, that still applies even if the PCs happen to be an all Rokea, Nuwisha, Gurahl, etc. game.<br /> <br /> So if the IC setting status quo ever changes, it simply takes away a tool from the ST in designing their chronicle and denies the PCs a (fairly unique) chance to be heroes in that chronicle who can bridge that distance. All the Fera either becoming good allies or complete enemies would be a poor setting design choice because it takes away options.<br /> <br /> Individual STs can come up with any scenario they want for their chronicles. An ambitious ST might even base an entire chronicle on the PCs precisely building ties with the other Fera. So there is nothing wrong with that scenario playing out in an individual game. <br /> <br /> It's just that the published setting itself should never do that. It needs to keep things nebulous with lots of different Fera NPCs with different opinions on the Garou (and vice versa) in order to present the STs the most tools with which they can customize their setting. You can have this sept here have excellent relations with the nearby Fera, and this other sept over there to have terrible relations, and others to be mixed. An ST can create lots of interesting, complex settings that way.<br /> <br /> Personally, I dislike the presentation of the War of Rage that it is all the Garou's fault. It denies any agency of the Fera themselves, ignores actual geography and animal range, and doesn't make much sense that decentralized Stone Age people could fight a global war (even with all the powers of the Garou) for many centuries. Localized conflicts with lots of different outcomes and motivations make better sense to me. That is why in my own chronicles, I present the War of Rage as a term created by Garou historians, and that the standard take of &quot;Garou bad, the Fera good&quot; is basically a morality tale the Children of Gaia use to bludgeon their political opponents inside the Garou Nation to accept their leadership instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T13:36:41-07:00","id":1540528,"title":"","content":"It's definitely possible, one of the main themes of Revised was attempts to rebuild the bridges with models like The Ahadi and The Beast Courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T13:42:26-07:00","id":1540529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540500-w20-garou-building-ties-with-the-other-fera?p=1540528#post1540528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's definitely possible, one of the main themes of Revised was attempts to rebuild the bridges with models like The Ahadi and The Beast Courts.</div> </div> </div> </div>i didn't know revised was like that, that's cool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 08-16-2024, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T07:57:00-07:00","id":1543858,"title":"","content":"It's possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T23:59:59-07:00","id":1543954,"title":"","content":"Absolutely. We have sections of the world like Asia, with the Beast Courts, where the shapeshifters never parted ways. And in Africa, the Ahadi are rebuilding ties after the Werelions basically carried out their own mini War of Rage slaughtered a ton of people. Of course, it's important to note that the War of Rage never really reached Asia or Africa to the extent that it did in Europe and North America or Australia. So in Africa and Asia, werewolves are generally outnumbered by other shifters. Meanwhile in the western world, the werewolves genocide has left other shifting breeds with far fewer in number and a lot more animosity. Further, especially in North and Central America, the War of Rage was being fought very recently - the Camaztoz were extermined in the 1600s and you had werewolf septs slaughtering other shifters within the last couple of centuries.<br /> <br /> In Europe and North America, the scars from War of Rage are much more recent, and many shifters in these parts of the world point to this as proof that the werewolves never learned from their mistakes. They carried out the War of Rage thousands of years ago, and then happily jumped back in as soon as they were given the opportunity.<br /> <br /> So it's definitely possible to bring the shifters together, but it's also going to be an incredibly difficult and legendary task.<br /> <br /> Also, I feel it's important to point out that with the War of Rage, while many shifters ultimately hold the werewolves as primarily responsible, many of them also hold themselves responsible to some degree for shirking their own duties. Like the Nagah believe the War of Rage is totally their fault and their society has undergone a lot of changes as a result of that guilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}